If it makes it any easier to remember, I was always confused by this until =
I
started thinking of {bo} differently

When I see {A .iXbo B} think of the X as describing how B relates to A.  So
{A .ibabo B} is "B is ba to A".  And {A .imu'ibo B} is "B is mu'i to A".

To me it seems like {.iXbo} is consistent between PU and BAI and it's the
forms {broda mu'i lo nu brode} and {broda ba lo nu brode} that are being
inconsistent with each other.  {A ba lo nu B} is "A after B" but {A mu'i lo
nu B} is "A because of B".

With BAI it seems like the selbri is static and we're just adding more
information to it "mi citka (oh and by the way the motivation for such
was...) mu'i lo nu mi xagji".  But PU reaches back and modifies the
information about the selbri "mi citka (oh but wait, I did that citka-ing
AFTER...) ba lo nu mi xagji".

2010/9/4 Jorge Llamb=EDas <jjllambias@gmail.com>

